Description: TinhMenhDo Ubuntu vanilla GNOME and Flatpak metapackage
 TinhMenhDo Ubuntu configures an Ubuntu desktop around the vanilla GNOME
 desktop packages, GNOME Software and Flatpak. It conflicts with Snap, the
 Ubuntu Dock extension and Yaru theme packages so APT cannot keep them
 installed alongside this profile. Adwaita is installed as the neutral GNOME
 theme/icon fallback. The Ubuntu wallpaper package remains required by
 Ubuntu's GNOME Shell package on supported releases and is not a Yaru theme.
 .
 This package deliberately does not purge user data, call apt recursively,
 add arbitrary third-party PPAs. It provides a Zsh setup with Oh My Zsh,
 common plugins, and persistent history. It also installs archive tools, Noto
 fonts, and the GNOME Extensions manager. It resets existing Ptyxis
 preferences once so the terminal starts from its default profile instead of
 inheriting an Ubuntu-specific palette. Fcitx5 is enabled at login, with
 SKey, Google Chrome Stable, Tailscale, and RustDesk are recommended where
 packages are available. Tailscale and RustDesk services are enabled at boot.
